      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "```\n\n2026.02.23 20:39:52 Warning    -  [Video Playback] ERROR: [youtube] sRi5E1_pAik: Sign in to confirm youï¿½re not a bot. Use --cookies-from-browser or --cookies for the authentication. See  https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/wiki/FAQ#how-do-i-pass-cookies-to-yt-dlp  for how to manually pass cookies. Also see  https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/wiki/Extractors#exporting-youtube-cookies  for tips on effectively exporting YouTube cookies\n\n```\n\nI think this can be fixed by VRChat updating yt-dlp to 2026.02.21 which pulls in yt-dlp-ejs 0.5.0 fixing sig extraction in the main player variant. VRChat currently uses yt-dlp 2026.02.04 / yt-dlp-ejs 0.4.0, with incompatible sig extraction. I made a feature request: [Update yt-dlp to 2026.02.21 to resolve YouTube playback issues](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/update-yt-dlp-to-20260221-to-resolve-youtube-playback-issues)",
